  "printed_contract": "W2(r_y,N(0,I)) <= sqrt(E_r_y ||grad rho_y||^2); first bound invokes Gaussian T2 plus Gaussian LSI. Binary entropy tensorization is omitted analytic background, not printed paper theorem.",
  "generic_objects": "Two actual probability measures on arbitrary measurable spaces; actual measurable bounded nonnegative F on product; Phi(t)=t log t, Phi(0)=0; A(x)=integral_y F(x,y), B(y)=integral_x F(x,y), m=integral F.",
  "mathematical_contract": "integral Phi(A)+integral Phi(B) <= integral Phi(F)+Phi(m), equivalently entropy subadditivity. Produce joint/all-slice/marginal L1 before algebra. Zero functions, positive-measure zero fibers and m=0 included; no normalization or positive lower bound premise.",
  "source_vs_authored": "SLT conditional entropy/duality/first-k telescoping route unbounded L1 class is external. Bounded delta-regularization/logsum/DCT is authored sufficient background alternative. Pointwise bounded measurable assumptions internally obtainable from later compact C2 squared observer; no implication from marginal DPI alone.",
